The Golden Sparrows are an [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oreskian]] movement against the government, made up largely of people who served in the Oreskian military and who carry over the intelligence service's way of writing messages. They break into [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]] offices and other government buildings for what they need, and to keep their own refuges from being found.

They pass word in plain sight: coded notices printed in newspaper circulars, and marks left on doorposts and stoops that only members can read. [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] and [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] belong to the movement, and Lev has done its killing; he murdered a writer who had written against the Sparrows, in a train station, with a pencil.

Their headquarters is in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Sarengrad|Sarengrad]]. They take an interest in the [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Kerneyy Prison Outpost|Kerneyy Prison Outpost]], because many of the prisoners held there are their own.
